cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the article it accompanies."
title: "analysis-scale-trials: code and derived results for the analysis-scale reanalysis"
abstract: >-
  Analysis pipeline, simulation, and derived summary results for a study of how
  an unrecorded choice of analysis scale changes what a randomized trial
  concludes, across 27 randomized trials and 1,445 post-randomization
  comparisons. Two scripts in reproduce/ need no credentials and no local data:
  reproduce_worked_example.py applies the pre-specified specification menu to a
  publicly redistributable trial and shows the mean-based P-value moving from
  0.029 to 0.353 while the rank-based P-value stays put, and
  reproduce_calibration.py reproduces the null floor that every observed rate
  must be read against. Contains no participant-level data: results/ holds
  endpoint-level summaries only, because two of the three trial sources are held
  under data use agreements that permit publication of aggregate results but not
  redistribution of records.
